### E0 window (LAG up, no event), 12:54:5x-12:56:40 box time
Port counters BEFORE (12:54:08, `show interface`): port1.0.1 in 1171599 out 1166251; port2.0.1 in 40 out 748;
  port3.0.1 in 1165514 out 1172012.
Run together: tools/tb sudotool tb101 lacp-1222 l2flows 100 100 /tmp/lacp-1222/flows-e0 bond0 eth2 (4 flows x 100 pps,
  12:54:5x-12:56:3x) ; linerate A: --tx bond0 --dst-mac 00:0d:b9:51:4d:a1 --rx eth2 --src-ip 10.37.101.34 --sport 5010
  --src-macs 16 --mac-prefix 02:cc:0a:00 --rate top --secs 60 ; linerate B: --tx eth2 --dst-mac 00:0d:b9:51:4d:a2
  --rx bond0 --sport 5011 --src-macs 16 --mac-prefix 02:cc:0b:00 --rate top --secs 60 (both 12:55:03-12:56:04);
  tools/tb capture eth3 35 s + eth4 35 s `ether proto 0x8809`.
  (--src-ip is needed on bond0, which has no IPv4; distinct --sport per direction because linerate's rx filter is
  `ip and udp src port N` and tcpdump sees the NIC's own transmissions too.)
Results:
- linerate A: sent 1879545 (374.9 Mbps frame bytes, 31326 pps; two concurrent senders share this host's CPU);
  rx eth2 1874531 (99.7%); linerate B: sent 2208726 (440.6 Mbps, 36812 pps); rx bond0 2207439 (99.9%).
- Port counters AFTER (12:57): port1.0.1 in 2131378 out 2422150; port2.0.1 in 939818 out 973929; port3.0.1 in
  3394240 out 3071563. Deltas: po1 IN = 959779 + 939778 = 1899557 = 1879545 (A) + 20000 (2 bond0 l2flows x 100 pps
  x 100 s) + 12; port3.0.1 OUT = 1899551 -> **the DUT forwarded every direction-A frame** (6 fewer = the host's
  LACPDUs/own frames, not forwarded). port3.0.1 IN = 2228726 = 2208726 (B) + 20000 exactly; po1 OUT = 1255899 +
  973181 = 2229080 (+354 = the DUT's LACPDUs and flooded frames) -> **every direction-B frame was forwarded**.
  Per-leg spread: A arrived 50.5%/49.5% on port1.0.1/port2.0.1 (the bond's layer2 hash); B left 56%/44%.
- Host NIC counters (tools/hostinfo.py --stats, new option): eth2 rx_fifo_errors 5054 (direction A short by 5014),
  eth4 rx_fifo_errors 1043 + eth3 248 = 1291 = bond0 RX dropped 1291 (direction B short by 1287). rx_missed 0,
  rx_no_buffer 0, crc 0 on all. **The shortfall is the host's own receive FIFO under two line-rate senders +
  two tcpdumps + l2flows on one box; the DUT lost nothing.** DUT counters are the authority for DUT loss; the
  host's tcpdump count is a lower bound. Consequence: the EVENT windows below run the line-rate pair at
  --rate 300 each way (a load the host receives cleanly: the controls at ~700 Mbps one way were 100%) so
  flowstat's outage timing measures the DUT and not this FIFO, then a `top` window per direction after each
  recovery.
- l2flows (flowstat-e0.txt): all 4 flows delivered with scattered 2-3-frame gaps (20-30 ms) and 0 dups; loopwin
  windows 0 (no frame delivered twice). The gaps coincide with the line-rate windows (host FIFO, above).
